sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Retrieval, reranking, and context selection
  accDescr: The notebook runs each query through FAISS and cross-encoder reranking. Fixed selection retains ten documents. Dynamic selection applies a relative threshold and falls back to the top document when nothing qualifies. Metrics evaluate retrieved context rather than generated answers.
  autonumber
  participant Run as Notebook
  participant Search as MiniLM and FAISS
  participant Rank as Cross-encoder
  participant Select as Selector
  participant Metrics

  Note over Run,Search: Corpus embeddings are indexed before evaluation
  Run->>Search: Encode query and retrieve 50 candidates
  Search-->>Run: Candidate document texts
  Run->>Rank: Score each query-document pair
  Rank-->>Run: Documents and scores, highest first
  Run->>Select: Apply the configured strategy
  alt Fixed K
    Select->>Select: Keep the first 10 documents
  else Dynamic K
    Select->>Select: Keep scores >= 0.8 x highest score
    opt Empty set
      Select->>Select: Keep the top-ranked document
    end
  end
  Select-->>Run: Selected context documents
  Run->>Metrics: Context plus known answer
  Metrics-->>Run: Answer presence, precision, MRR, NDCG, word count
  Note over Run,Metrics: Repeat for 30 synthetic queries under each strategy
